{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"[operator-attested] Final Gerrit/CI completion evidence and rebar-debug report. Problem/root cause: two reliability tests encoded production-scale real-time values—a 10s low-speed window/15s loopback server and a 1s per-attempt deadline plus real 2s/4s retry sleeps—despite contracts about throughput, retry schedule, process count, and cleanup rather than elapsed seconds. Held-out `/tmp/rebar_short_window_oracle.py` was RED on current main for both exact nodes, GREEN after repair (2 passed in 3.88s), RED again when the socket mutation restored window=10/server=15, and independently RED when the ACLI mutation restored the 1s deadline; restoration returned GREEN. Fix: real loopback traffic now runs above the floor for 2s across an injected 1s window; the ACLI test installs 0.1s call/grace/drain during fixture setup, records logical `[2,4]` without sleeping, launches exactly `_MAX_ATTEMPTS` real sessions, records each parent-side `Popen.pid`, and polls until all PIDs are absent. Production defaults are byte-unchanged. Current-main replication: held-out oracle passed; both full files passed 20 tests in 10.53s; Ruff/format, project mypy across 527 files, diff-check, and ticket resolution passed. GitHub Actions run 31752047186 (https://github.com/navapbc/rebar/actions/runs/31752047186) completed SUCCESS at 2026-08-13T23:25:43Z with all Ubuntu/macOS cells green; Gerrit change 1748 received LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, zero unresolved comments, and is MERGED as a79ed876b00d15682f27ceedf3d072ac1a4c72f5 on origin/main. No assertion, real socket/process boundary, attempt, cleanup proof, dependency, platform, Python version, mutation, coverage, or runner was removed. OSS match: CPython dd1194e and urllib3 52dfb19 use short injected trigger windows with generous cleanup. End-to-end observation: this no-macOS-queue run took 27m46s versus 34m12s immediately before; macOS took 26m43s versus 33m10s. That 6m26s improvement is observed but not attributed solely to the ~20s of directly removed waits because suite/runtime variance remains. Siblings/parity: the scoped socket and subprocess tests were both fixed; production timing surfaces remain unchanged and no additional parallel surface is missing the rule."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786663615215716001,"uuid":"70f550dd-3d9b-4598-a717-2a0b406087dc"}